CORE
main.c
--no-por --unwind 2 --rounds 3 --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Two threads store, under a mutex, to different members of one node through
pointers loaded from the enclosing struct. Neither store may reset the other
thread's member to a stale value: the leaves a store does not meet are not
published, so reading them without an event is safe.
